IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-nouns`
IMPORT `nsw-dictionary`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 1 Preliminary: sections 3, 4 and 5.
-- Sections 1 (short title) and 2 (the Act's own commencement) are machinery and have no rule here.
-- Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else ("the contrary intention appears"), the judgment is a plain input.

§ `Part 1 Preliminary`

§§ `3 Definitions`

-- src:28 | (1) In this Act—
-- src:29 | instrument means an instrument (including a statutory rule or an environmental planning instrument) made under an Act, and includes an instrument made under any such instrument.
@ref s 3(1) instrument (src:28-29)
GIVEN `it is an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under another instrument that is within this definition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the thing is an instrument within the meaning of this Act` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument`
    THEN JUST (`it is made under an Act` OR `it is made under another instrument that is within this definition`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:31 | (a) a reference to a function includes a reference to a power, authority and duty, and
@ref s 3(2)(a) (src:31)
GIVEN thing IS A FunctionLike
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(a) a reference to a function includes a reference to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN APower THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnAuthority THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ADuty THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnotherKindOfFunction THEN NOTHING

-- src:32 | (b) a reference to the exercise of a function includes, in relation to a duty, a reference to the performance of the duty.
@ref s 3(2)(b) (src:32)
GIVEN thing IS A FunctionLike
      `the reference is to the performance of the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(b) a reference to the exercise of a function includes a reference to` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN ADuty THEN IF `the reference is to the performance of the duty` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN APower THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnAuthority THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherKindOfFunction THEN NOTHING

-- src:33 | (3) The Dictionary in Schedule 4 defines certain terms used in Acts and instruments.
@ref s 3(3) (src:33)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE DictionaryEntry
`s 3(3) the Dictionary in Schedule 4 defines the term` MEANS
    `Schedule 4 the entry for the term` term

§§ `4 Act binds Crown`

-- The Crown in right of New South Wales, or the Crown in any other capacity.
DECLARE CrownCapacity IS ONE OF
    CrownInRightOfNewSouthWales
    CrownInAnotherCapacity

-- src:35 | 4 Act binds Crown
-- src:36 | This Act binds the Crown in right of New South Wales and, in so far as the legislative power of Parliament permits, the Crown in all its other capacities.
@ref s 4 (src:35-36)
GIVEN capacity IS A CrownCapacity
      `the legislative power of Parliament permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN CrownInRightOfNewSouthWales THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN CrownInAnotherCapacity THEN JUST `the legislative power of Parliament permits it`

§§ `5 Application of Act`

-- src:39 | (1) This Act applies to all Acts and instruments (including this Act) whether enacted or made before or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 5(1) (src:39)
GIVEN kind IS A TextKind
      `it was enacted or made before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN AnActText THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AStatutoryRuleText THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnEnvironmentalPlanningInstrumentText THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnotherInstrumentText THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:40 | (2) This Act applies to an Act or instrument except in so far as the contrary intention appears in this Act or in the Act or instrument concerned.
@ref s 5(2) (src:40)
GIVEN `the contrary intention appears in this Act or in the Act or instrument concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` MEANS
    NOT `the contrary intention appears in this Act or in the Act or instrument concerned`

-- src:41 | (3) Wherever appropriate, this Act applies to a portion of an Act or instrument in the same way as it applies to the whole of an Act or instrument.
@ref s 5(3) (src:41)
GIVEN `it is a portion of an Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3) this Act applies to the portion in the same way as to the whole` MEANS
    IF `it is a portion of an Act or instrument`
    THEN JUST `it is appropriate`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:42 | (4) Nothing in this Act excludes the application to an Act or instrument of a rule of construction applicable to it and not inconsistent with this Act.
@ref s 5(4) (src:42)
GIVEN `the rule of construction is applicable to the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is inconsistent with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(4) this Act leaves the application of the rule of construction in place` MEANS
    IF `the rule of construction is applicable to the Act or instrument` AND NOT `the rule is inconsistent with this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:43 | (5) This section does not authorise a statutory rule to exclude or modify the operation of Part 6 (statutory rules and certain other instruments).
@ref s 5(5) (src:43)
GIVEN kind IS A TextKind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(5) section 5 authorises the statutory rule to exclude or modify the operation of Part 6` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN AStatutoryRuleText THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN AnActText THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnEnvironmentalPlanningInstrumentText THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherInstrumentText THEN NOTHING

-- src:44 | (6) The provisions of sections 24, 28, 29, 30, 30B, 33, 42, 43, 69A, 75 and 80 that apply to a statutory rule also apply to an environmental planning instrument.
@ref s 5(6) (src:44)
GIVEN section IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(6) the provision that applies to a statutory rule also applies to an environmental planning instrument` MEANS
    IF elem section (LIST "24", "28", "29", "30", "30B", "33", "42", "43", "69A", "75", "80")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests: Part 1`

-- s 3(1): an instrument made under an Act, or under another such instrument; one made under neither is not.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the thing is an instrument within the meaning of this Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the thing is an instrument within the meaning of this Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the thing is an instrument within the meaning of this Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the thing is an instrument within the meaning of this Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(2): "includes" lists three things and does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) a reference to a function includes a reference to it` APower EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) a reference to a function includes a reference to it` AnAuthority EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) a reference to a function includes a reference to it` ADuty EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(a) a reference to a function includes a reference to it` AnotherKindOfFunction EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) a reference to the exercise of a function includes a reference to` ADuty TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) a reference to the exercise of a function includes a reference to` ADuty FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b) a reference to the exercise of a function includes a reference to` APower TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(3): the Dictionary's entry for a term, and a term it does not define
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the Dictionary in Schedule 4 defines the term` "month" EQUALS JUST `Schedule 4 'month'`
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the Dictionary in Schedule 4 defines the term` "week" EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` CrownInRightOfNewSouthWales FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` CrownInAnotherCapacity TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` CrownInAnotherCapacity FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(1)
#ASSERT `s 5(1) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` AnActText TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` AnActText FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` AStatutoryRuleText TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` AnEnvironmentalPlanningInstrumentText FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` AnotherInstrumentText FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 5(2)
#ASSERT `s 5(2) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2) this Act applies to the Act or instrument` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 5(3)
#ASSERT `s 5(3) this Act applies to the portion in the same way as to the whole` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(3) this Act applies to the portion in the same way as to the whole` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(3) this Act applies to the portion in the same way as to the whole` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(4)
#ASSERT `s 5(4) this Act leaves the application of the rule of construction in place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(4) this Act leaves the application of the rule of construction in place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(4) this Act leaves the application of the rule of construction in place` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(5)
#ASSERT `s 5(5) section 5 authorises the statutory rule to exclude or modify the operation of Part 6` AStatutoryRuleText EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(5) section 5 authorises the statutory rule to exclude or modify the operation of Part 6` AnActText EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(6): the eleven listed sections, and one that is not listed
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the provision that applies to a statutory rule also applies to an environmental planning instrument` "24" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the provision that applies to a statutory rule also applies to an environmental planning instrument` "30B" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the provision that applies to a statutory rule also applies to an environmental planning instrument` "69A" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the provision that applies to a statutory rule also applies to an environmental planning instrument` "80" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(6) the provision that applies to a statutory rule also applies to an environmental planning instrument` "36" EQUALS NOTHING
